  "Pre-existing child edges that already satisfied rule 1 and were left alone: PAP-239->243, PAP-240->247, PAP-239->248, PAP-240->250.",
  "Extras (2): PAP-268->276 and PAP-51->276 encode hard dependencies PAP-276 names in text (PAP-35, PAP-51) that were not parent blockers. PAP-257->225 was planned and dropped (see relationsSkipped).",
  "Rule 2: 57 'last child blocks D' relations. Where a parent has several leaf children the leaf was chosen by relevance and recorded in 'why': PAP-57 -> PAP-224 (auth UI completes end-to-end login); PAP-59 -> PAP-229 for the 10 UI/API dependents and PAP-228 for PAP-39 and PAP-163 (SQL predicates); PAP-81 -> both PAP-244 and PAP-245 (gate 2 needs all three reviewers); PAP-45 -> PAP-273 for PAP-47/48/50 because PAP-273's text says it blocks them (the compose stack is the real dependency), PAP-275 -> PAP-54.",
